[{:db/id 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1fae684a-7e13-519a-aef1-3caa737a3e69"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339084 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186382270 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1\\}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-1fae684a-7e13-519a-aef1-3caa737a3e69" :question/id #uuid "1fae684a-7e13-519a-aef1-3caa737a3e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-72178" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{3}\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:      \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $-\\frac{1}{2}$ to $\\frac{1}{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}[{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can also swap the order of integration. This gives \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1/3}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe184e8e-6c3d-5fe7-aa56-1a1728b67c6b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe184e8e-6c3d-5fe7-aa56-1a1728b67c6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe184e8e-6c3d-5fe7-aa56-1a1728b67c6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8ea7f02-d0bc-58f0-b333-df298335e3ed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c9577fe-e0ea-5924-a5a3-56d0d5cd71b2" "answer-f8ea7f02-d0bc-58f0-b333-df298335e3ed" "answer-dec4c0cb-7929-5b16-9e0e-753322768bf1" "answer-5f04548b-c5b2-5dd6-91f7-ac226f8ce5f1" "answer-be4791cb-b433-5220-a3ae-6b3c2cac9bc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c9577fe-e0ea-5924-a5a3-56d0d5cd71b2" :answer/id #uuid "6c9577fe-e0ea-5924-a5a3-56d0d5cd71b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8ea7f02-d0bc-58f0-b333-df298335e3ed" :answer/id #uuid "f8ea7f02-d0bc-58f0-b333-df298335e3ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dec4c0cb-7929-5b16-9e0e-753322768bf1" :answer/id #uuid "dec4c0cb-7929-5b16-9e0e-753322768bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f04548b-c5b2-5dd6-91f7-ac226f8ce5f1" :answer/id #uuid "5f04548b-c5b2-5dd6-91f7-ac226f8ce5f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be4791cb-b433-5220-a3ae-6b3c2cac9bc7" :answer/id #uuid "be4791cb-b433-5220-a3ae-6b3c2cac9bc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129843 :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $1$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $1$ to $3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128539 :answer-field/correct 17592186128543 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}]
